--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` excludes this PR from its sibling
scan only through the `SELF_PR_NUMBER` environment variable, which only
`.github/workflows/CI.yml` sets. Run interactively from a worktree whose branch
already has an open PR, it reports that PR's own ticket as a rival claim:

    COLLISION: ticket ID 1089 is also added by open PR #1374 (branch t1084-roar-close-and-clean).
    exit 1

Observed on 2026-10-12 while checking the `t1084-roar-close-and-clean` branch
before a merge decision. CI is unaffected — it passes
`github.event.pull_request.number`. The exposure is an agent that runs the gate
locally, believes the report and renumbers a ticket that never collided, which
breaks the ticket ID and every cross-reference to it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] With `SELF_PR_NUMBER` unset, the script resolves its own PR from the current branch (forge call marked `harness-extension-point`) and excludes it; when the branch has no open PR it scans the full sibling list
- [x] Run from a worktree whose branch has an open PR adding a ticket file, it exits 0 with that PR excluded, verified against a real open PR
- [x] Positive control: a genuine sibling collision is still reported when two open PRs add the same ID and the script runs from one of them
- [x] `make check` passes

## Raid plan — 2026-10-13

Actions: preserve explicit SELF_PR_NUMBER and the no-ticket fast path; infer this PR from the marked open-PR list lookup plus the proven local origin repository/current branch when unset. An inspection failure is not proof of no PR: fail closed and never recommend renumbering on an uncertain self claim. Update forge-coupling documentation.

First test: unset SELF_PR_NUMBER; own PR claims the added ID, a sibling claims a distinct ID; expect exit 0 and no own-PR file fetch. Positive control: sibling claims same ID and is named with exit 1. Cover no matching open PR, repository/list inspection failure, override, foreign same-name siblings and ambiguity. Validate against a real open PR as required.

Files: scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh; tests/test_check_cross_pr_ticket_collision.sh; this ticket. Dependencies: git, gh, jq and existing hermetic shell fixtures. No new library. Exit criteria unchanged.

## Validation evidence — 2026-10-13

- Real open PR #1374 (`t1084-roar-close-and-clean`, head `aa4850dea8ecdbc5017900537a579d4708db3303`) adds 1089/1090: isolated checkout, unset SELF_PR_NUMBER, exit 0. Final simplified inference uses the actual open-PR list and origin-repository lookup, exits 0 and excludes its own claim.
- Hermetic open-PR controls exclude own #99 and report sibling #77 for ID 0300 (exit 1). Single foreign-fork #55 with the same branch name also reports a collision; same-name own and foreign PRs are distinguished by source repository identity. Missing source identity and ambiguous self both fail closed without renumber advice.
- Updated affected shell suite passes; `make check-fast`: 964 passed; declared adherence `make lint`: 182 passed. Final simplified full `make check`: 1603 passed, 4 skipped (84.02s); structural checks passed.
